# Normalise every text file to LF *in the repository*.
#
# Without this only *.sh was managed, so a Windows checkout was free to commit
# CRLF. v1.15.0 did exactly that: DEPLOYMENT.md, the four READMEs, settings.py
# and ~25 other files landed on `development` with CRLF while `main` still held
# the LF originals. Git then sees every single line as modified, which is what
# made the testing -> main PR (#40) conflict across whole files at once.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text vs binary (binaries contain NUL bytes and are
# left untouched); `eol=lf` pins the in-repo form. Working-tree endings on
# Windows are unaffected for editing purposes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they break inside the Docker containers.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never touch these, regardless of what auto-detection thinks.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
